+### Browser tests (optional, a separate lock)
+`requirements-browser.in` lists two direct pins: `playwright==1.63.0` and `pillow==13.0.0`. Two lock files made with uv 0.11.32, each with hashes and each held to the pins of the matching development lock (`-c`), so installing it after the development lock changes no development pin: `requirements-browser.txt` (`uv pip compile requirements-browser.in --generate-hashes --python-version 3.12 --python-platform linux --no-strip-extras --exclude-newer 2026-11-12 -c requirements-dev.txt -o requirements-browser.txt`) and `requirements-browser-win.txt` (the same with `--python-version 3.13 --python-platform windows`, `-c requirements-dev-win.txt` and `-o requirements-browser-win.txt`). `--exclude-newer` ignores any release uploaded after that date, so the same command gives the same lock later. Install: `pip install --require-hashes -r requirements-browser.txt` after `requirements-dev.txt`. The checks in `.github/workflows/lint.yml` do not install it (no browser job yet).
+
+| Package | Version | Licence (the package's own metadata) | Used for |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| playwright | 1.63.0 | Apache-2.0 | drives the browser in the browser tests |
+| pillow | 13.0.0 | MIT-CMU (licence expression in its metadata; the wheel carries a `LICENSE` file) | one test reads a screenshot's pixel colours |
+| greenlet 3.5.6, pyee 13.0.1 | | MIT AND PSF-2.0 (greenlet), MIT (pyee classifier) | transitive of playwright |
+| typing-extensions 4.16.0 | | PSF-2.0 | transitive of pyee; the same pin as in the development lock |
